ce:section.ce:para:
Two-stage fermentation of food waste was performed at lab scale CSTR in two systems, comprised of a hydrolysis reactor and a methane reactor. The reactors had a total volume of 5L with an internal diameter of 0.15m and a height of 0.4m. The working volume was 1.35L for the hydrolysis reactor and 4.0L for the methane reactor (Fig. 1
                        ). A third system, a single-stage reactor with the same dimensions as the methane reactor of the two-stage system was also employed (Fig. 2
                        ).
